  "source": "read-only snapshot of actual worktree; upstream untouched",
  "adaptations": [
    "Serialized mapping, local BA and loop closure; no upstream worker threads are started.",
    "Time-sampled keyframes accept static scenes.",
    "SuperPoint/SuperGlue supplies ordered stereo correspondences and float descriptors; cosine image signatures retrieve candidates.",
    "Only landmarks with at least three observing keyframes and verified multi-frame reprojection enter localization.",
    "One-pixel Huber pose refinement, geometric outlier removal and refit; minimum support and image coverage are checked.",
    "Visual corrections update immediately after geometric validation; odometry-origin clustering is removed.",
    "Grid point creation and global per-cell deletion are removed; distinct SuperPoint features retain their identities.",
    "Fix reset ownership, deferred deletion return values, initialized erase state, and external query keyframe IDs.",
    "Initialize every stable keyframe pose, and share the production frame transaction between threaded and synchronous entries, including deferred deletion cleanup.",
    "Restore all-observation landmark reprojection validation instead of the upstream unconditional success.",
    "Native-scale SuperPoint projection uses octave zero and no ORB pyramid distance gate.",
    "Enable robust head pose optimization against mature shared-map landmarks and a single ratio-tested association window.",
    "Use origin-invariant camera-position and rotation agreement for loop acceptance, fuse geometrically verified loop landmarks, and refit accepted wrist image observations against optimized map landmarks after every map transaction.",
    "Skip invalid landmark anchors during pose graph updates and release transient projection caches.",
    "Protect the two active wrist reference keyframes from culling until their references are released; commit map revisions across all three camera corrections before geometry transport.",
    "Refit head pose after robust outlier rejection; preserve active wrist anchors even when deletion was queued before acceptance.",
    "Verify wrist localization with two agreeing map references before accepting a pose; expose mature-landmark head pose support for reliable relocalization.",
    "Share robust reprojection refinement between fresh localization and retained-image map updates; verify image coverage and camera-centred, depth-normalized pose observability, requiring ten retained inliers for map updates."
  ],
